.TH MFM 1 2026-11-18 mfm "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mfm \- minimal file manager for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mfm
.RB [ \-h | \-v ]
.RI [ directory " | " file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
mfm shows one folder as a list in the look of the Motif window manager, with the
colours of mwc.
Without an argument it starts in the current directory; given a file, it opens its
folder and selects it.
If the start directory cannot be opened, it shows
.B $HOME
and gives the reason in the status line.
.PP
Commands act on the marked entries, else on the selected one.
Marks belong to the current folder and survive the automatic reload; changing
folders, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X and a plain click drop them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Print the usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Anything else that starts with
.B \-
is refused, the usage goes to stderr and the status is 1; a file named so is given as
.BR ./\-name .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End
Move, on the keypad too.
.TP
.B Return
Open a folder, or a file with
.BR MFM_OPEN .
.TP
.B Right
Open a folder.
.TP
.B Backspace, Left, Alt+Up
The parent folder.
A parent that may be traversed but not listed is skipped.
.TP
.B Alt+Home
The home folder.
.TP
.B letters
Jump to the next name starting with what was typed, ignoring case, umlauts included.
After a second without a key the search starts over.
During a search Space is part of the name.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Enter a path.
Typing
.B /
or
.B ~
first starts over.
.TP
.B F2
Rename.
The name without its extension is selected: typing replaces it, Left and Right place
the cursor.
.TP
.B F7, Ctrl+Shift+N
New folder.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Show or hide hidden files.
.TP
.B Ctrl+1, Ctrl+2, Ctrl+3
Sort by name, by size with the largest first, or by date with the newest first.
The same key again reverses the order.
Folders stay on top, by name among themselves when sorting by size.
Entries of equal size or date are by name.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R, F5
Reload.
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
A terminal in the current folder.
.TP
.B Space, Insert
Mark or unmark, then move to the next row.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Mark all, or unmark all.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X
Remember the entries for copying or moving, inside mfm.
.TP
.B Ctrl+V
Paste into the current folder.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Put the entries into the clipboard of the session, for other programs, and leave what
Ctrl+V pastes as it was.
They are offered as
.B text/uri-list
with
.B file://
URLs, which Firefox pastes as files, as
.B x-special/gnome-copied-files
for GNOME's file managers, and as plain text, one path per line, unless a name is not
valid UTF-8 or has a control character such as a newline in it.
When the clipboard cannot take them, the marks stay.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Send the entries with
.BR MFM_SEND .
.TP
.B Delete
Move to the trash.
.TP
.B Shift+Delete
Delete permanently, after asking:
.B y
or
.B j
confirms, any other key cancels.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the search, else the message, else the marks.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q, Ctrl+W, Alt+F4
Quit.
Under mwc the compositor takes Alt+F4 and closes the window.
.PP
In the input fields for the path, a rename and a new folder, Left, Right, Home and End
move the cursor, Backspace and Delete delete, Ctrl+U clears, Return confirms and Esc
cancels.
.PP
Only moving and typing repeat when held: Up and Down, in the list and the menu,
letters, and in input fields also PgUp, PgDn, Left, Right, Backspace and Delete.
During a search Backspace and Space repeat too.
Everything else acts once per press: holding Backspace goes up one folder, holding
Space marks one entry.
.SH MOUSE
A click selects and unmarks everything, a double click opens, Ctrl+click marks,
Shift+click marks the range up to the selection.
The wheel scrolls, and leaves an input field or the question before deleting open;
the scroll bar can be dragged or clicked into its trough.
The arrow button and button 8 go to the parent folder.
A click into the path field edits it.
.SS Context menu
Button 3 in the list opens a menu with Open, Cut, Copy, Copy to clipboard, Paste,
Send, Rename, Move to trash, Delete permanently, New folder, Terminal, hidden files and
Reload.
Send is there only with
.BR MFM_SEND .
.PP
On a marked entry the marks stay: the commands act on all of them, while Open and
Rename are offered only with at most one mark.
On any other entry the menu selects just that one.
On empty space it acts on the marks, else on the folder.
While a background job runs (see below), Paste, Rename, Move to trash, Delete, New
folder and Send are off.
.PP
Press, drag onto a command and release, or click it; Up, Down and Return work too.
Esc or a click elsewhere closes the menu.
If the listing changed while the menu was open, the command does nothing.
.SH FILES AND FOLDERS
.SS Background work
Copying, moving, permanent deletion and Ctrl+S run in a background process, and the
window stays usable.
Another such action, F2 and F7 included, is refused until the running one is done.
Quitting mfm does not stop it.
The status line shows the result or the first error.
After Ctrl+X the remembered entries that could not be moved stay, to paste again;
all of them stay when the background process dies.
.SS Nothing is overwritten
Within a file system, moving is a rename that never replaces an existing name.
Copies and moves across file systems are made with
.B cp \-a
(on FAT and exFAT, which keep no permissions,
.BR "cp \-R \-\-preserve=timestamps" )
and first land in a hidden folder
.B .mfm\-XXXXXX
in the target and are renamed from there, so half a copy never shows under the real
name.
If the name is taken, also in different case on FAT, a copy is called
.IR "name (copy).txt" ,
.IR "name (copy 2).txt"
and so on, a moved entry
.IR "name (2).txt" .
That is also how Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V in the same folder makes a duplicate.
mfm refuses to copy or move a folder into itself, and a rename onto a taken name.
.PP
A move across file systems removes the original only once the copy is in place.
If the copy fails, for example on a full disk, it is cleaned up and the original stays
as it was.
If the original cannot be removed completely, the status line says so; the copy is
complete.
.SS Deleting and the trash
Permanent deletion is
.BR "rm \-rf \-\-one\-file\-system" .
Mount points and folders with something mounted in them are refused, for deleting and
for the trash.
.PP
The trash follows the freedesktop.org specification, so any file manager that knows it
restores from it; by hand, the files are in
.B files/
and their original paths in
.BR info/*.trashinfo .
It is
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash
(default
.BR ~/.local/share/Trash ).
Files on other file systems go to
.B .Trash/$UID
at their root, if the administrator set up a shared
.BR .Trash ,
else to
.BR .Trash\-$UID ,
with the path relative to that root.
What is in the trash already is not trashed again.
Where trashing fails, as on a read\-only file system, Shift+Delete is left.
.SS The listing
The folder is checked for changes every second and read again, keeping the selection
and the scroll position; one that takes long to read is checked less often.
If it disappears or becomes unreadable, mfm moves to the nearest readable parent.
A changed size or permission alone does not count; Ctrl+R shows it.
.PP
Paths are logical, as with
.B cd
in the shell: after entering a linked folder,
.B ..
leads back to the folder the link is in, and a terminal from Ctrl+T gets that path as
.BR $PWD .
.PP
File names that are not valid UTF\-8 are shown as Latin\-1.
Control characters, bidirectional controls and characters that do not show, such as a
soft hyphen, show as U+FFFD, so that a name cannot pose as another one or as one with
another extension.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mfm/mfmrc
(default
.BR ~/.config/mfm/mfmrc )
is written like mwc's mwmrc: one
.B Mfm*key: value
per line,
.B Mfm.key
and any case work too, a line starting with
.B !
is a comment, and the last line for a key wins, also one with a value too long to
keep, which then counts as none.
mfm never writes it.
.BR open ,
.B send
and
.B terminal
are read on each use; the rest at startup.
.TP
.BR open ", " send ", " terminal ", " font
The same as
.BR MFM_OPEN ,
.BR MFM_SEND ,
.BR MFM_TERMINAL ,
.BR MFM_FONT .
.TP
.BR background ", " activeBackground
Window and selection colour.
Default:
.B Mwm*background
and
.B Mwm*activeBackground
from
.BR ~/.config/mwc/mwmrc .
.TP
.BR foreground ", " activeForeground
Text on the window and on the selection.
Default:
.B Mwm*foreground
and
.B Mwm*activeForeground
from mwc's mwmrc, else black or white, whichever reads better.
.TP
.B sort
.BR name ", " size " or " date :
the order mfm starts with.
.TP
.B sortReverse
.BR true :
that order reversed.
.TP
.B showHidden
.BR true :
start with hidden files shown.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
A set variable wins over its mfmrc entry.
.TP
.B MFM_OPEN
Opens files; default
.BR xdg\-open .
The file is the last argument.
.TP
.B MFM_SEND
Ctrl+S, for example
.BR adb\-push\-download .
It gets all paths at once as its last arguments and runs in the background like a copy;
the status line shows success or its first error line.
.TP
.B MFM_TERMINAL
Ctrl+T.
Default mwc's terminal,
.B MWC_TERMINAL
or
.B Mwm*terminal
in mwmrc, which runs with
.BR "sh \-c" ,
as mwc runs it;
else the first found of foot, xterm, uxterm, x\-terminal\-emulator, urxvt, alacritty,
konsole, kitty, xfce4\-terminal and gnome\-terminal.
.TP
.B MFM_FONT
A Pango font name such as
.BR "Sans Bold 11" ;
default
.BR "Sans 10" ,
and 10 points without a size.
Fontconfig patterns such as
.B Sans:size=10
are rejected.
.TP
.BR MWC_INACTIVE ", " MWC_ACTIVE
Window and selection colour, as for mwc; default
.B #aeb2c3
and
.BR #7387ad .
.PP
.BR MFM_OPEN ,
.B MFM_SEND
and
.B MFM_TERMINAL
are split into words at spaces, and quotes group words, as in
.BR "xterm \-fa 'DejaVu Sans Mono'" .
There is no shell syntax beyond that; a small script can provide it.
The program is looked up only in the absolute entries of
.BR $PATH ,
never in the folder shown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg\-open (1)
